<title>HONG KONG: HK bourse amends rules for listed banking firms.</title>
<headline>HK bourse amends rules for listed banking firms.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Stock Exchange of Hong Kong said on Tuesday it has amended listing rules to require listed banking companies to include cash flow statements, segment information and market risk information in their annual accounts.</p>
<p>The amendments apply for accounting periods ending on or after December 31, 1996, the exchange said in a statement.</p>
<p>Banking companies include banks, restricted licence banks and deposit taking companies.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
